---
description: Hipohipo login, automatic conversation capture, and background document saves
alwaysApply: true
---

Use this plugin's MCP tools for Hipohipo memory and library operations.
Automatic conversation capture is handled by Hooks. Do not reconstruct or
summarize history and call `memory.write` as a substitute. Use that tool only
for a separate memory operation required by the user's task and its tool contract.
An accepted history upload does not establish successful memory extraction.

Ordinary MCP tools stay available before and after login. Use them directly:
foreground operations obtain or refresh authorization before dispatch.
The conditional source.parse_background tool requires current server permission.
Status is passive and does not start login. Complete browser consent when
requested. After cancellation, failure or logout, use `auth.login` only when the
user explicitly requests another login. Pending means the operation was not
executed; it is not replayed after the call ends. Platform activation and trust
remain controlled by the app.

For an explicit save with insufficient write permission, explain the permission
requirement. For a proactive save, skip silently when permission is unavailable.
Hipo resolves the destination from current authorization; never
infer or choose a Project from local paths or previous conversations. Local
collection continues before login and after logout; valid authorization is
required to upload. Disabling Hooks stops collection. Other Hipohipo plugin
clients may share the system-stored grant; do not promise that logout affects
only this installation. Independently authorized HTTP MCP grants are separate.

Use `/hipohipo-status` or the bundled `status` command for capture counts and
coverage. Report only relevant diagnostics. Do not print credentials, transport
URLs, or conversation content for routine status checks. Do not inspect
credential stores or the capture database, search old conversations, or look
for a `STATUS.md` file; this plugin does not generate one.

Do not trigger document capture for installation guides, Agent instructions,
source code, or configuration read, created, or edited to perform an engineering
task, unless the user explicitly asks to save those files to Hipohipo. Read or
edit them directly without library calls. Determine
scope from the user's task and file reference; do not ask for confirmation to
decide whether the file is in scope.

Load document-capture before first reading supplied documents or when writing
standalone plan, report or design files. Follow it through `source.parse_background`
before the first reading or final file delivery, when the tool is advertised.
Plans awaiting approval or implementation can be complete deliverables, including
engineering documents stored in a repository. Do not create files from chat text
just for capture. Remember capture attempts in this conversation: repeated reads,
ongoing edits and later revisions must not trigger another background call.
Resume existing pending operations; only an explicit user request permits another
save or parse. Different complete paths are new candidates; do not track renames.
If absent, denied or unavailable, skip the save and continue the original task
without login, extra prompts or fallback to `source.create`. Drafts and
intermediate revisions are excluded. Use `source.create` for an explicit user
save request. An explicit instruction not to upload or save externally takes
priority; skip saving and continue the original task.

If background parsing returns `confirmation_required`, the path was previously
uploaded to the current Project and no new Source or upload was created. Ask
whether to parse the current version again. Only explicit agreement permits
`source.create`; otherwise continue without another attempt or repeated question.
Do not alter the path, metadata or retry key to bypass confirmation. This is not
a fallback for an absent, denied or unavailable background tool.

For background companion reads, call `library.list` and `source.get_status`
with `{isBackground: true}`. If unavailable, keep the admitted Source and
operation identifiers and continue without login, preparation or an ordinary-read
fallback. User-explicit reads omit this hint.

Choose a matching existing folder from `library.list` when available; otherwise
use Library root. Do not create folders automatically or ask a folder question.
Retain exact document references and immutable revisions, account and Project
destination, idempotency keys, Source and operation identifiers. Resume admitted
operations instead of creating duplicates after uncertain submission. Use
`source.get_status` and report the actual outcome before claiming success.

MCP receipt updates invalidate a subscribed resource; reread it for current
state. Do not treat the notification itself as successful completion or promise
an automatic Agent response. Hook capture acknowledgements are internal
submission IDs, not MCP operation receipts.
